From: Sakovich, Aaron <ASakovich@ncs.com>
Subject: New XL models!

Hello ANTers,

Has anyone else noticed the pricing and configuration info on the two new   
Alpha XL models announced by Digital a couple days ago?  The 366 MHz   
system is just under $10K, and the 300 MHz box is $8.5K -- this pricing   
is better than the clone manufacturers using the same processor!

The other interesting thing I noticed is that the memory bus is now 128   
bits wide (of course, this still contrasts with some of the other boxes   
with 256 bit wide memory busses).  What's so fascinating about this is   
that all the other Celebris and Alpha XL models had 64 bit wide memory   
busses.  I would hazard a (somewhat educated) guess that this means the   
motherboard needs to be swapped out for an upgrade -- that it's not   
strictly a daughtercard change.  (That is, unless Digital has started   
putting the memory on the daughtercard...)  SIMMs should now have to be   
added in 4's -- does that mean the slot count on the mb has gone from 6   
down to 4, or up to 8?  Eight slots with 64 MByte SIMMs would equal the   
announced capacity of 512 MBytes.

And one other piece of good news, the PowerStorm graphics adapters are   
now supported on NT.

Just some wild thinking to ease my braincells...

Aaron
