From abauch@email2.hlo.dec.com Wed May  1 12:58:39 1996 CDT
Message-ID: <960501134425.625@email2.hlo.dec.com.0>
Date: Wed, 1 May 96 13:44:26 -0400
From: Aaron Bauch <abauch@email2.hlo.dec.com>
Subject: Re: New XL models!

>The other interesting thing I noticed is that the memory bus is now 128   
>bits wide (of course, this still contrasts with some of the other boxes   
>with 256 bit wide memory busses).  What's so fascinating about this is   
>that all the other Celebris and Alpha XL models had 64 bit wide memory   
>busses.  I would hazard a (somewhat educated) guess that this means the   
>motherboard needs to be swapped out for an upgrade -- that it's not   
>strictly a daughtercard change.  

Your somewhat educated guess is correct.  While the chassis remains the
same, the 21164 upgrades (either 300 or 366MHz) change both the baseboard
and CPU card, while using the same memory SIMMs.  This tradeoff occurred
since keeping a 64 bit bus would have been a bad move for performance
and keeping the ability to upgrade existing systems was a very high
priority (ie: keep the box at the very least).  The result is a very
good balance of these two objectives.

By the way, while I work for Digital, my information is strictly
third hand as a member of another organization than the one that builds
the XL product line so please take this for what it is worth and not
an "official" Digital statement.  Thanks

Aaron

