Subject: RE: NT 3.51 Mac File Server Performance

--Boundary (ID UFZqRvzgYXikcvN4jUA/7Q)
Content-type: TEXT/PLAIN

Run the performance monitor with logging turned on.  Monitor the   
Processor object.  Turn on each screen saver one at a time while placing   
bookmark at the beginning and end of each screen saver test.

It may make more sense to you when you see the amount of processor used   
by the 3GL screen savers.  It may be possible that the MAC File Services   
need more processing time and are therefore more affected by the screen   
saver used.

When only use the basic logon screen savers on our server.  We also   
recommend simple screen savers on our workstations as complex ones   
brought our enterprise wide backups to a standstill !!  Hope this helps.

Tim Bailer
tim.bailer@jhuapl.edu

