I'm afraid that this is one of _the_ most obvious things to check on NT.
As a backup vendor, we hear time & time again about strange performance
issues, and we ask what is running on the server at the time of the backup.
"Nothing."
"Are you sure ?"
"Absolutely nothing."
"Are you positive."
"Yes. Nothing other than the screen saver, of course".
"Ah ha!"
"You realize of course that that 3D Pipes screen saver is sucking the will
to live out of your CPU don't you at 99%?"
"uh.....no".

I'm sorry I didn't suggest the obvious, but that is what is overlooked
the most frequently.  DOH!

