From: Terry - think pc, Think Pc, THINK PC! <donald@wrksys.ENET.dec.com>
Subject: Re: New XL models!

Hi,

The Alpha XL 233 and 266 use longword parity to protect the data in memory.
These systems don't need as many memory bits on the SIMMs, so 33-bit
SIMMs can be found in these models.

The Alpha XL 300 and 366 use ECC to protect memory data. They require 36-bit
SIMMs. The 300 and 366 have up to two banks of memory (four SIMMs to a bank).

>Your somewhat educated guess is correct.  While the chassis remains the
>same, the 21164 upgrades (either 300 or 366MHz) change both the baseboard
>and CPU card, while using the same memory SIMMs.  This tradeoff occurred

Regards,
