Alpha 233. As the subject line hints, I'm grappling with the idea of =
local client apps rather than serving up the apps centrally.

Here's the situation. I'm entering a Lab environment which has approx. =
200 WFW nodes. Currently, all applications run locally on each node. =
These machines range from 486 50s to P100--all with 16mb of ram. One =
thing to note is that the labs run a maintenance utility called Rdisk. =
Its an application that runs a checksum comparison replacing files that =
are not included in templates.

The School has recently purchased an Alpha 233 with 128mb of ram. Please =
note that I come from an environment that was completely opposite this =
situation with all applications running off a central server. I intend =
to enforce the usual security controls but am uncertain whether its =
worth it to move applications to the server.=20

