Date: Fri, 3 May 1996 14:44:56 -0700
From: Paul Bunn <paul@beicorp.com>
Subject: Re: how to obtain scsi device info on alpha/nt?

At 02:44 pm 05/03/96 -0400, bsweeny wrote:
>Hi,
>
>I have an AlphaServer 1000 running NT Server v3.51 sp4. It has a DEC 
>KZPAA-AA scsi adapter which connects to a Storageworks BA350 shelf 
>containing three RZ28B's and a TZ87N. 
>
>How can I determine the scsi address settings for these disk and tape  
>devices from a running NT system? Shutting down the machine just to 
>query the bus is not an option. Thanks in advance - Brian
>

Run the Registry Editor, REGEDT32 and view the following:

Hkey_local_machine   window:
hardware\devicemap\scsi\scsi port x\scsi bus y\target id z\logical unit id 0

where x=0 for your first adapter
y=0 for the first bus on your adapter
z=scsi id

Hope this helps.

Regards
Paul Bunn, Barratt Edwards International Corp. (BEI)
