From: James Livingston <jwl@ntmail.zso.dec.com>
Subject: RE: Alpha Crashes about once a week

Rich,

The first thing you should do is update to 3.51.  When you prepare to do
that, you should look at your firmware version number, and upgrade it to
what's on the Digital NT Web page,
http://www.windowsnt.digital.com/default.htm.  At this moment, that's
version 4.47 of the NT ARC firmware.

Just for background, once a new version of Windows NT ships, Microsoft
are not much interested in the problems of the previous version.  That
will be doubly true for version 3.5 when version 4.0 ships, and you will
likely have to go through an upgrade to 3.51 before you can install 4.0
as an upgrade, as well.  The point of this story is, don't wait to
upgrade, if you can help it.  

What I don't quite understand is what you're asking in your third
question.  The only sure method I know of to update from 3.5 to 3.51 is
to plop the 3.51 CD-ROM in the drive, select "Supplementary menu...",
and then "Install NT from CD-ROM", choosing to upgrade the present
system, rather than installing a new one.  

Cheers,
James

