Subject: Re: NT4 and Visual C++ 4 debugger

Jean-Luc,
     
     >>I recently installed NT 4.0 beta and encounter the follwing problem.
     >>In Microsoft Visual C++ 4.0 (MSDEV), the call stack window is alway 
     >>empty.
     
     >>Any idea ?
     
     Getting Visual C++ 4.0 and the Windows NT 4.0 Beta1 Working
     Together on Digital Alpha Systems
     
     If you have a Digital Alpha system with Visual C++ 4.0 installed,
     and you upgrade your operating system to Windows NT 4.0 Beta1,
     Visual C++ may exhibit one or more of the following symptoms:
     
     * The Debugger Call Stack window fails to display the call stack.
     * The Debugger Variables Context combo box is empty.
     * Access violations frequently occur  when exiting the
       debugger (especially on large projects).
     * Access violations occasionally occur upon exiting the Developer
       Studio without using the debugger.
     
     These problems can be eliminated by copying the IMAGEHLP.DLL file
     from the Visual C++ 4.0 CD-ROM to the Developer Studio installation
     on your system.
     
     To copy the file:
     
     1. Open the BIN folder within your Developer Studio base folder. 
        The base folder's name is typically MSDEV.  
     2. Insert the Visual C++ 4.0 CD-ROM into your system's CD-ROM drive.
     3. Open the REDIST folder within the MSDEV folder on the CD-ROM.
     4. Drag and drop IMAGEHLP.DLL from the redist folder on the CD-ROM
        to the BIN folder on your hard drive.
     
     
     I hope this helps,
     
     Gary

