     This is the latest information from the Product Manager -- Development 
     Environment for Windows NT Alpha here at Digital...
     
     Visual C++ V4.1 for ALPHA is not marketed as a product or a
     subscription issue, but it is provided as a patch to VC++ V4.0 for
     ALPHA.  Therefore, although it identifies itself as Visual C++ V4.1,
     it is officially known as patch VC40AALPHA.
         
     New boxes of Visual C++ V4.0 will have the VC++ V4.1 CDs instead of 
     the VC++ V4.0 CDs, but customers who have the VC++ V4.0 CDs can get 
     the newer CDs by calling Microsoft support and requesting patch 
     VC40AALPHA.
         
     There might be a cost for media.
         
     Customers can tell if they have the VC++ V4.1 kit by:
     1. the VC++ V4.1 CD has a volume label of VC40AALPHA
     2. the VC++ V4.1 CD has a top level directory of TGS, which is not
     present in the VC++ V4.0 kit
     3. the "About Developer Studio" dialog identifies itself as VC++ V4.1 
     
     V40AALPHA won't be shipped until next week.
     
     Bottom line: RISC users are getting the new version for the cost of
     materials. (If MS chooses to charge. We're not sure of that yet.)
         
     
