From dthorpe@subliminal.com Fri May 10 00:57:44 1996 CDT
Message-ID: <199605100544.WAA10320@scruz.net>
Date: Thu, 9 May 1996 22:44:33 -0700 (PDT)
From: Danny Thorpe <dthorpe@subliminal.com>
Subject: Re: Converting from FAT to NTFS

At 09:38 AM 5/10/1996 +1000, you wrote:
>Hi all,
>        could someone let me know whether there is a way to convert the
>disk partition with NT on it from FAT to NTFS without having to reinstall.
>
> -Bruce Young

Use the Convert command line utility to convert the FAT file system to NTFS.
It'll convert the file system and preserve the files in place the next time
you boot NT.  See the "convert" help topic in winnt.hlp.

Note:  On RISC machines like the Alpha, the boot partition *must* be FAT.
The recommended installation is to make a small (2MB?) FAT partition for
your C: boot partition, and partition the rest of your hard disk as a second
logical drive, which you can then make NTFS.  Do not use convert on your C:
partition!

-Danny

From garmour@minnie.hollins.edu Fri May 10 07:20:47 1996 CDT
