Date: Fri, 10 May 1996 07:52:44 -0400
From: Gilbert Armour <garmour@minnie.hollins.edu>
Subject: RE: Converting from FAT to NTFS

At the command prompt run convert.exe /? to get the necessary syntax.  If 
this partition contains NT, then it will give you a message that you cannot 
convert the partition.  It then asks if you want it scheduled to run during 
the next system boot. Answer yes and next time you reboot it will convert 
to NTFS.

