Confounded for a moment, and then blissful realization of what must be
happening.  A normal disk format differs from a "quick format" in that it
scans for bad sectors.  A raid array maintains the bad sectors of it's
drives internally, and will therefore will immediately return a good status
on all sectors, without invoking any I/O to the array's disks.
If you have any RS Escort Cosworths spare, please send one to the
usual address.<g>

