Subject: RE: Performance on Alpha vs. Intel

I've installed 1 Intel and 2 Alpha NT servers (I know it's not many), one 
Alpha had to be reinstalled due to failed HD.  The Alpha install is very 
easy, once you procure the updated firmware and ECU utility.  As an Intel 
person, I have to admit the Alpha was just as easy even with a few extra 
steps.

I strongly suggest getting the NT Resource Kit.  It does a good job of 
explaining the process and comes with many nifty utilities on the CD-ROM. 
 We are converting from PATHWORKS to NT by the way.

For benchmarks I'd suggest DEC's homepage.  The important question is what 
will you use the server for?  You may not need the extra horsepower 
available on the Alpha and could avoid the extra cost by going Intel.  Or 
do what we're doing and mix the two.  We've had no problems mixing them.

