Ah, two different problems.  You'd asked for a way to disconnect users.   
 To limit the access to a share (before you do your NET SESSION /DELETE),   
you'll need to do a NET SHARE sharename /USERS:# where # is 0 if no one   
is to access it, or 1 if only your administrative access is to be   
allowed.  You can also completely turn off sharing on your server if you   
want to disallow any access to the system by doing a NET PAUSE SERVER; to   
restore, do a NET CONTINUE SERVER.

