NT Servers set up as Domain Controllers do NOT have the power users =
group, that only appears on Workstation and Server [set up as server].  =
You can set up a "dummy" global group, call it anything you'd like and =
bring it into the local Power Users group.  Anyone in the global group =
will have Power User priveleges on that system...

