From ASakovich@ncs.com Mon May 13 17:41:27 1996 CDT
Message-ID: <1996q2-0193.alphant@archive.invalid>
X-Archive-Original-Message-ID: <31976C1D@smtpgate.eagan.ncs.com>
Date: Mon, 13 May 96 11:11:00 PDT
From: Sakovich, Aaron <ASakovich@ncs.com>
Subject: RE: Remote Control

owner-alphant wrote:
>     Mornin'
>
>     Does anybody know of a good remote control utility for AlphaNT?  I   
am
>     thinking of something like pcAnywhere.
>
>     Justin Malcolm

Check out RCMD and RCMDSVC in the 3.5/3.51 resource kit (the 3.5 version   
is in the archive, but it's HUGE).  It will allow you to execute remote   
commands a la rsh/rexec or create a remote command shell from one NT box   
to another.  A telnet server is another possibility, and Seattle Labs has   
a version (again, a demo is on the archive.)

Kermit 95 has a telnet server facility -- watch for my upcoming review of   
the product to find out more about that (I've not gotten that far yet!)

Aaron

