Subject: error message on installation

Has anyone ever had a problem installing NT on an alpha machine?  I was
running 3.5 on a 21164 based system, and was having trouble with the machine
crashing.  The OEM suggested that I buy the 3.51 (full version, not just the
upgrade) and do a clean reinstall.  When the software finally arrived, I
started the installation
procedure - step by step according to their instructions.  Every time I get
to the point where the install program boots from the hard drive, I get a
blue crash screen with the message INACCESSIBLE_BOOT_DEVICE.  I have two
hard drives - both of which were known good before the new installation.  I
tried installing on the other drive and got the same results.  I tried
re-installing 3.5 just to get the system up and running and work on the 3.51
problem later - but at the same point in the installation procedure 3.5
generates the same crash screen with a
THIS_SYSTEM_MAY_BE_INFECTED_WITH_A_VIRUS message.  Strange - this particular
machine is not hooked up to a network or a modem, both hard drives have been
re-formatted numerous times (trying different ways to get the install to
work), and no floppies are used in it that are not either brand new or are
software installation floppies.  I can copy files from the CD-ROM to either
hard drive with the ARCSBIOS, and do
a file listing and see the files showing up on the hard drives; it just
won't complete the NT installtion.  Both the vendor and OEM are being little
or no help at all.  A thousand thanks to anyone who can suggest anything I
can try.  I really don't think I have a hardware problem; but it's a
possibility.

