Subject: BAPCo benchmarks

forwarded from Paul Hakala:

AlphaNt Users,

	I work for Digital Equipment Corporation and one of my responsibilities
is to represent Digital on BAPCo which is a consortia consisting of 20
or so different hardware and software vendors with the objective of
developing benchmarks to measure performance. For those that aren't familiar 
with  BAPCo  you can access the web site at http://www.bapco.com to find out  
all the information you would ever want to know. 

Briefly BAPCo is a benchmarking consortia that uses  real applications
(commercially available applications either through wholesale/retail 
distributors) as part of the suite. Version 1.0 includes Microsoft Word, Excel
and Powerpoint, MAXeda from Orcad and Texim Project from Wellcom Software. 
