Subject: RE: Multi-Processor Alphas

Daryl,

I'm not sure what you're asking about, specifically, but Digital Alpha
systems are available in 1-4 processor (SMP) systems, specifically the
AlphaServer 2100/2100A families; processors can be either 21064A, at
speeds of 233 MHz or 275 MHz, or 21164, at speeds of 250 MHz or 300 MHz
(processors must all be the same type and speed).  Memory can go up to 2
Gbytes on these systems (limits you to 3 processors).  

You can certainly run Windows NT Workstation on any Alpha system you
have, AlphaServers included, though they are normally sold with Windows
NT Server.  There are also systems that cost somewhat less and run only
one or two processors, the AlphaServer 2000 family; they also can run
Workstation.

If this doesn't get at what you want, please feel free to elaborate your
question.

