>         What we'd like to be able to do is have our VMS systems
>         initiate file transfers to our NT server via FTP, so
>         nightly production jobs can make data available to our
>         users.  Users can initiate FTP sessions from their desktops,
>         but what software do we need to have the FTP session
>         started (automatically) from VMS to NT?
> 
>         Thanks for any suggestions...
> 
>                                                 -- Judy

Hi Judy,

FTP Server is included in NT Workstation -- you'll need to add the FTPSVC
software and set it up.

job that will run on a schedule to copy your files down to the client.
Note that you'll need UCX v3.3 ECO 6 or later, as I recall -- there was
a problem with scripting ftp prior to that.

Alternatively, you could also start the scheduler on all your NT boxes, and
schedule an AT job from the client side.

Personally, I've not given up on PATHWORKS yet -- the server side is "free",
includes NetBEUI and TCP/IP support, and an FPA license for the client is
only $99.  Being able to access files via UNC, with security, netlogon
authentication, long file name support, plus integration with Explorer
(oops, I'm running NT 4.0, so in most cases, that would be File Manager)
gives me a lot more freedom.  Plus the VMS systems can act as BDC's for
my NT server PDC.  My $.02...

Aaron

