Subject: RE: NT Server support for multiple subnets

Yes you can, but DHCP binds to the first IP address on the NIC.  So have 
two options that I know of:  1) Install a NIC for each subnet supported 2) 
Define the server's subnet mask to cover both subents.  Option 1 will 
maintain separate nets and the server will route between them.  Option 2 
sees one net and will not route between subnets.

