What you may want to consider is using some smaller, less capable system =
set up to be your Domain Controller.  An i486 can easily handle 750 =
users when it is only doing duty as a PDC or BDC.  Then set your 2100 up =
as a SERVER not a DC.  I assume from your email address that these users =
will be hitting this system for database apps [not MS SQL6.x!].  In this =
case get your drive subsystem as fast as possible, either RAID 3 [faster =
reads] of RAID 5 should do it.

Hope this helps some.
