This is what I cannot stand about ARCserve -- they bypass all normal channels
of talking to the tape drive, and talk to the tape drive direct.  This means
that
you are reliant on Cheyenne (as you have found out) for driver support, and it
also means that you cannot use ANY other application (including even ntbackup!)
if you have ARCserve installed.  What's worse is that if you buy a tape
drive with
NT certification, there is absolutely no guarantee that it will work with
ARCserve.

You will probably find that the ncrc810.sys file from SP1 broke ARCserve.  Try
replacing this file (\system32\drivers) with the copy that came from your NT CD.
You will need to type
EXPAND (cd-rom):\alpha\ncrc810.sy_ (nt-dir)\system32\drivers\ncrc810.sys
to do this.

