Folks,
	I work for Digital Equipment Corporation and one of my responsibilities
is to represent Digital on BAPCo which is a consortia consisting of 20
or so different hardware and software vendors with the objective of
developing benchmarks to measure performance. For those that aren't familiar 
with  BAPCo  you can access the web site at http://www.bapco.com to find out  
all the information you would ever want to know. 

Briefly BAPCo is a benchmarking consortia that uses  real applications
(commercially available applications either through wholesale/retail 
distributors) as part of the suite. Version 1.0 includes Microsoft Word, Excel
and Powerpoint, MAXeda from Orcad and Texim Project from Wellcom Software. 
The development of 1.0 started over 2 years  ago when  applications for NT
were limited and scarce. The committee at that time used whatever applications
they could get a hold of with the  required license agreements. Now since
NT  is gaining market share and applications are becoming more available,
we decided to do a second version (2.0) that would be more representative  on 
how NT is being used in the market place today.  

The committee is working on a survey to be used to determine  which applications
should be used in the next suite. The committee decided it would be more
beneficial to interview a list of companies that are currently using NT today
representing all the  major market segments.  I need to come up with a couple
of names of customers that would be willing to be interviewed to determine
their NT usage. We hope to find out through the interviews what applications
they use, how they use them, how much they are used and which ones are most
important in their work. 

The committee broke everything  into segments (Banking, Finance, Manufacturing,
Retail, Medical, Education, Engineering etc..) I was assigned  to get some 
contacts in the Engineering segment.  I also will be responsible for writing 
the  section of the survey for  ECAD/MCAD. I need  to generate a list of 
questions to ask for that  specific category. (i.e. what functions to you 
commonly use,  how big are your data sets etc...) 
 
If anybody would be willing to be interview or could give me some  pointers 
to people that may be of some  assistance, in identifying customers that we 
could talk to and help in the development of the ECAD/MCAD section of the 
survey it would be  greatly appreciated. You can send me mail or
call at the number below.

My specific responsibility for this survey is the ECAD/MCAD area ( the work
gets divided among all the members) but I will be willing to talk to anybody  
in  any market segment. 

Thanks in advance for your help.

Regards,
