Disclaimer: I possess biased opinions!

It's unbelieveable that a major player such as Cheyenne took this route.
The technique they used is called SCSI PASS-THROUGH and it is a terrible
design paradigm breach in my opinion to use it.  But why did MS put in there
in the first place ?  The reason is that it makes talking to esoteric SCSI
devices
simple via DeviceIoControl() calls which have no drivers.  But NT has excellent
tape drive support, so Cheyenne had no excuse not to use them.  In fact their
approach immediately rules out QIC tape drives which ARE on the HCL!!  Future
technology such as USB will also not work with ARCserve, until it is re-written
to accept it -- even if the manufacturer releases an NT driver for it.

