Scott,
 It's hard to tell what you're actually referring to....No you won't be =
able to browse the Mac's under file manager's connect to network =
drive......

There are basically two pieces to the "Services for Mac" under NT =
Server.
The File Server let's NT Server appear as a Mac file server on the =
network.  You can create shared volumes that PC, NT-RISC and Mac clients =
can "see".  You've got to have an NTFS partition in order to do this, =
though.  You can define security for files and users, even require Mac =
users to have to log in and use a password to be able to access the =
shared volumes.
The Print Server for Mac is the other piece.  In here you can allow PC =
and NT-RISC clients to print to Appletalk PostScript printers [is this =
what you mean by two way?] Or let Mac clients print to any shared =
printer on the network.  Mac clients printers are controlled by the NT =
server and the Mac print jobs must go thru it to print.

 RAS currently doesn't do anything with AppleTalk, maybe some newer =
version of Server will adress this....

Hope this helps.
cjm

p.s. This doesn't even address the possibilities of straight TCP/IP =
between Macs and NT Server!

