Date: Fri, 24 May 96 18:34:00 PDT
From: Sakovich, Aaron <ASakovich@ncs.com>
Subject: RE: Upgrading an Aplhastation 200 4/166

owner-alphant wrote:
>We have an Alphastation 200 4/166 that we would like to upgrade with a   
faster
>processor.
>
>Is it possible ? Is it worth ?  What does it implies in terms of   
hardware
>remplacement and cost?

Digital has a part number for the upgrade -- you can replace the 21064   
with a 233 MHz 21064a.  The kit also includes a new oscillator and name   
plate; the price to go from 166 to 233 (or from 100 to 166) is $2,995.

I've looked and haven't been able to find the upgrade part number,   
however.  You might have some luck by calling 800 DIGITAL.  If Digital   
has discontinued the upgrade program, you can still do it by getting your   
own 21064a, a new oscillator, and skip the name plate. <g>  Anyone on the   
mail list ready to venture a peek inside their Mustang 233 for a look at   
what the oscillator is?  Oh, yeah -- there's a jumper that needs to be   
switched, too.  Your owner's manual tells you which one that is.

Good luck,
Aaron
