Andy,
You have at least two options that I know of.   the NET USER command from 
an NT command window allows one to add accounts.  You could use a text 
editor to insert net user commands into your tab delimited file and save it 
as a .bat file which can then be executed.  

If you can convert your file to a comma-delimited file, than an even better 
solution is to use the ADDUSERS.EXE utility thats included in the NT 
3.51  resource kit. It reads directly from a comma-delimited file.

Scott...

