From: Nicholas Johnson <njohnson@dentalxchange.com>
Subject: Re: Mac File capabilities

I just set this up on our system.  Here's what I found out:

First, you must have an NTFS partition to be able to share files with a Mac.
Then go to the control panel and open the Network icon.  Press the Add
Software button and select Services for Macintosh and follow the
instructions.  You must then create a New Zone inorder for the Macs to
locate the server.  Then create an account for each person that will be
connecting.  This process should add the "MacFile" to the file manager and
the control panels.

--Nick

