Subject: FW: Raptor Reflex 400Mhz Alpha

I can say with some authority that the entire Reflex product line from DTI is
astounding in its performance numbers.  It will run Pro/E and many other NT
Alpha apps faster than anything else on the market, bar none.
The 433MHz has been recently announced into the reseller channel and 
500MHz systems were rather prominently on display in a number of places 
at the [US] National Ass'n of Broadcasters show here in Las Vegas, NV.  The
Reflex comes standard with six 32 bit PCI slots, 8 72-pin SIMM sockets, 4 fast
serial and 2 parallel ports + sound capability. [and a three button mouse for
Pro/E.....].

Pricing has gone crazy throughout the marketplace - as witnessed by the literal
 dumping by SGI on the r5000 based systems with Power Animator or the Web
 Development suite.  I suspect DEC maybe slow to react, but DTI's systems 
typically hit the market MONTHS before the equivalent DEC system and 
usually at prices that are QUITE competitive.

DTI's primary focus has been in the 3D Animation and Digital Video marketplace.
When you've got to appeal to customers that are used to Amigas and PCs that's a
tough sell and thus IMHO the pricing is artificially depressed for systems of this
capability.  There apparently are server products in the works from DTI - I saw 
that on their web page, www.dti.com -- this isn't NDA kind of stuff,  but I could
probably speculate with some degree of accuracy on this topic - and I expect
these to shake up the market as spectacularly as any of DTI award winning
products.

As a side note, DTI does NOT use the same support chipset as DEC, they have
their own.......as well as their own ARC-BIOS.  IMHO this is HARDLY a deterrent
in anyway toward purchasing any system from DTI, since their chipset has proven
to be LESS BUGGY than the Alcor [& other derivative] chipset from DEC.  These
systems ARE on the MS HCL, pass NT3.51 AND NT4.0 B2 Hardware Compatibility
Tests with ease.

If you have any further questions please feel free to contact me  -- I hate to appear
evangelical about a product line.....sorry [esp to sjg]

